sketch-orca oracle patch 0006: the front end's objects in full, under SKETCH_ORCA_ORACLE_DUMP.
Modified for Sketch, 2026-11-07.

With SKETCH_ORCA_ORACLE_DUMP=<folder> (patch 0005), front-objects-<n>.sop1 holds all the front end
has once the objects are placed, so that the Rust translation's preset loading, model loading and
placement can be checked at that boundary (parity/SOP1.md):
- a CONF "run" after the RUN record: run()'s config at that point, load_settings' config with
  place_prime_tower's wipe_tower_x and wipe_tower_y (the call becomes
  dump_front_objects(model, cfg));
- a PCGC record: the plates' custom G-code (Model::plates_custom_gcodes) and the current plate;
- for each model object, after its MODL and CONF records: an HRNG record, its height ranges
  (layer_config_ranges), then a CONF "model-height-range" for each range; a BRIM record, its brim
  ears (brim_points); and a PNTV record for each volume, its painting (the TriangleSelector data
  of its supports, seams, colours and fuzzy skin).
It reads no knob of its own. A dump folder that does not exist stops the oracle before it does
anything else, with exit code 78 (patch 0005). Unset, nothing is written and nothing changes.

